diff --git a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
index 3e64607..f2e5bea 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
@@ -174,3 +174,35 @@ Run ``python3 tests/mt6762/test_lab_display.py --qemu build/qemu-system-aarch64
 readback faults and rejected pipeline-write tests. Native XNU integration
 uses the separately packaged ``prepare.py --native-lab-display`` option;
 its assertions must never be copied into a real phone's loader handoff.
+
+Opt-in power and mailbox laboratories
+------------------------------------
+
+``lab-power=on`` independently adds synthetic PWRAP WACS2 and keypad MMIO.
+PWRAP transactions follow a timed idle/busy/read-valid/clear sequence. The
+only writable PMIC registers are the two ADC request bits; unknown writes
+are rejected. Fixed, explicitly synthetic battery and thermistor conversions
+become ready after virtual-time delays. No battery physics, calibration,
+charging safety, fuel gauge, rail management or real keys are simulated.
+``lab-key-mask`` accepts bits0/1/2 for power/volume-up/volume-down levels.
+``lab-power-fault`` supports ``none``, ``stall``, ``init-loss``, ``bad-id``,
+``adc-timeout``, ``adc-rail`` and ``keypad-disabled``. Read-only
+``lab-power-state`` reports requests, completions, clears and rejected writes.
+A stalled transaction does not recover just because its fault is removed.
+
+``lab-sspm=on`` adds only the mailbox0 data/control register interface.
+The exact PLATFORM ``0xdead,0,0`` liveness command receives a synthetic
+response; CPU-DVFS commands remain unsupported and receive no success ACK.
+W1C acknowledgement preserves unrelated bits. ``lab-sspm-fault`` supports
+``none``, ``timeout``, ``ack-stuck``, ``input-stuck``, ``stale-ack``,
+``stale-input``, ``dead`` and ``wrong-ack``. ``lab-sspm-state`` separately
+counts requests, responses and ACK clears and states ``dvfs_emulated=false``.
+The default board maps neither fixture. Enabling either one is immutable
+after initialization; their fault properties are dynamic for testing.
+
+Independent tests are ``tests/mt6762/test_lab_power.py`` and
+``tests/mt6762/test_lab_sspm.py`` with the same ``--qemu`` and ``--dtb``
+arguments as above. Native-loader options ``--native-lab-power`` and
+``--native-lab-sspm`` grant only the corresponding synthetic ownership and
+verification assertions. Their successful guest execution is distinct from
+real phone power, battery, buttons or SSPM firmware validation.
